{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will bless those who bless you.</b> Do not think in your heart, saying: I have no relative or redeemer in the land. For I love you, I will love, and those who hate you I will hate." "<b>And I will bless those who bless you, and him who curses you I will curse.</b> And if you ask: in another place we find that the curse preceded the blessing, as it is written, ״אורריך ארור״. Because the righteous — their beginning is suffering and their end is tranquility. Rather, one may answer: the verse opens with blessing first, as it is written, ״והיה ברכה,״ and since it stands in the context of blessing, it also states ״ואברכה מברכיך״ and only then states ״ומקללך אאר.״ <b>And him who curses you.</b> Singular form, to teach you that those who bless are more numerous than those who curse. [And him who curses you I will curse — Abraham was well known as beloved, and not many will curse him; therefore its form is written in the singular.] <b>ונברכו</b> — light stem (פעל), like ״מברכך ומרכיב״ (Shevi'it 2:6), that is, through you the families of the earth's nobles will intermingle, and you will not be accounted as a foreigner and stranger among them, and therefore it writes here משפחת האדמה."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:59.816570424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}